.TH CSTR_APPEND 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cstr_append \- append a C string, and call _ccol_fatal_err() on failure
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

cstr_append(s, str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro calls cstring_append(), and when that call gives anything
other than ccol_success it calls _ccol_fatal_err().
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s     cstr to change
str   C string to append (must not be NULL)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
If you want to handle an error yourself, call cstring_append() directly.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_append (3),
.BR cstr_prepend (3),
.BR cstr_insert (3),
.BR cstr_set (3)
